          "path": "_m/9/q/8/y/fort-funston-wp/bluffs-at-fort-funston-in-san-.jpg",
          "filename": "Bluffs at Fort Funston in San Francisco (8507203970).jpg",
          "caption": "Sometimes taking a shot in the dark reveals the light of day. My first wide field astrophotography related self portrait shot along the bluffs at Fort Funston in San Francisco, Ca. I sat in the moonlight facing the Pacific Ocean gazing into the night sky searching for Cassiopeia and the Andromeda Galaxy and decided to take some shots hoping to capture celestial delights by the light of the moon. It turns out i found what i was searching for. Enjoy!\n\nLighting courtesy of the full moon (99% full)",
          "alt": "Sometimes taking a shot in the dark reveals the light of day. My first wide field astrophotography related self portrait shot along the bluffs at Fort Funston in San Francisco, Ca. I sat in the moonlight facing the Pacific Ocean gazing into the night sky searching for Cassiopeia and the Andromeda Galaxy and decided to take some shots hoping to capture celestial delights by the light of the moon. It turns out i found what i was searching for. Enjoy!\n\nLighting courtesy of the full moon (99% full)",
          "width": 697,
          "height": 1048,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "jason jenkins from stockton, california",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bluffs_at_Fort_Funston_in_San_Francisco_(8507203970).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "fort-funston-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "9q8y",
